---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "April 28, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — Bible Seek"
  description="The terms under which Bible Seek is offered."
  path="/terms"
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-accent">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink leading-tight"
    >
      Terms of Use
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div
      class="prose prose-neutral mt-10 max-w-none text-ink-soft leading-relaxed [&_h2]:font-serif [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_p]:my-4 [&_a]:text-accent [&_a]:underline"
    >
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of the Bible Seek iOS application and
        the website at bibleseekapp.com (together, the "service"). By
        downloading or using the service you agree to them. If you don't
        agree, don't use the service.
      </p>

      <h2>The license you have</h2>
      <p>
        Bible Seek is offered free of charge for personal, non-commercial
        use. You may install and run the app on iPhones you own or
        control. You may not redistribute, repackage, decompile, or sell
        the app or its bundled assets.
      </p>

      <h2>Scripture sources</h2>
      <p>
        The King James Version (1611) and American Standard Version
        (1901) are in the public domain. Lexicon data is adapted from the
        OpenScriptures Strong's project, also in the public domain.
        Specific citations and credits live on the
        <a href="/#about-credits">About → Credits page in the app</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>User content</h2>
      <p>
        Highlights, notes, bookmarks, and other annotations you create
        belong to you. They never leave your device. We claim no rights
        to your annotations.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided "as is" and "as available" without
        warranty of any kind. While we strive to ship a reliable app,
        scripture is the canonical source — please don't rely on the app
        for time-critical or salvific decisions without consulting a
        physical Bible and your community.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Bible Seek and its
        creator are not liable for any damages arising out of your use of
        or inability to use the service.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes
        will be reflected in the "Last updated" date. Continued use of
        the service after a change constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@bibleseekapp.com"
          >hello@bibleseekapp.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
